AEMS — Licensing (PLACEHOLDER — NOT YET FINALIZED)
==================================================

The Autonomous Energy Monitoring System (AEMS) is intended for release as open
hardware and open-source software. The specific license terms are still being
finalized and WILL be committed here before/at publication.

Planned licensing split
------------------------

AEMS is a mixed hardware + software + documentation project, so different parts
are expected to carry different licenses:

  * Hardware design files (hardware/)      -> open-hardware license   [TODO]
  * Firmware and host software (firmware/) -> open-source software    [TODO]
  * Documentation and figures              -> documentation license   [TODO]

Each SPDX identifier and full license text will be added here, and per-directory
LICENSE files will be placed where appropriate, once the choice is confirmed.

Third-party components
----------------------

Vendor and third-party components retain their own licenses, including but not
limited to:

  * STMicroelectronics STM32H7xx HAL / CMSIS / BSP drivers
  * FreeRTOS
  * OpenAMP / libmetal
  * FatFs
  * BlueNRG-2
  * Third-party KiCad symbol/footprint libraries under hardware/CustomLibs/Downloaded/

See the LICENSE / license headers distributed with those components (e.g. under
firmware/Drivers/ and firmware/Middlewares/). Nothing in this file overrides the
terms of any third-party component.

Interim terms
-------------

Until the final license(s) are committed, please contact the authors before
redistributing or reusing the AEMS design files or software.

Contact: Sangkee Min <sangkee.min@wisc.edu>; Vignesh Selvaraj <vselvaraj@wisc.edu>
Department of Mechanical Engineering, University of Wisconsin–Madison.
